 come the feature debut of the most exciting talent in South America. After cutting his teeth on the short film festival circuit with LA MUJER ROTA (2012), TOOTH FAIRY (2017) and LA HORA AZUL (2022), Jermias Segovia now bursts on to the international scene with  a gritty shocker. A family plans to murder their daughter’s killer after he is released from a twenty-year prison sentence. Still pleading innocence, the ex-convict tries to rebuild his life until the ghosts of the past return to haunt him  </p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1784579629361temp-1784579629296-cover.jpg\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2026\",\"runtime\":\"93\",\"language\":\"Uruguay\",\"country\":\"Uruguay\",\"premiere\":\"UK\",\"rating\":\"18\",\"genre\":\"Spanish\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Jeremias Segovia\",\"cast\":\"Esteban Bigliardi, Javier Chavez, Eduardo Miglionico, Mirella Pascual\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-07-20T12:56:25.632Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-07-25T11:37:53.561Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true}],\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-19T12:04:04.512Z\",\"is_virtual\":false,\"comscore_include\":true,\"geographic_restrictions\":[],\"geographic_exclusions\":[],\"vague_geographic_restrictions\":false,\"show_in_coming_soon\":false,\"allow_preorder\":false,\"aarp_member_required\":false,\"show_quantity_countdown\":false,\"virtual_balloting_enabled\":false,\"virtual_balloting_inline_during_playback\":false,\"use_default_event_bucket_preroll\":true,\"virtual_content_preroll\":[],\"virtual_content_preroll_visible\":true,\"use_default_event_bucket_postroll\":true,\"virtual_content_postroll\":[],\"virtual_content_postroll_visible\":true,\"virtual_intervals\":null,\"display_ads\":[],\"images\":{},\"custom_email_text\":\"<p>Thank you for your order.&nbsp;Please find below your ticket. You just need to produce this on your phone where a member of our team will scan it.&nbsp;<strong>Please arrive on time – there are no trailers.&nbsp;Latecomers may be denied entry.</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>PLEASE NOTE:- FrightFest is a horror, fantasy, science fiction and thriller film based event for over 18s. Films shown will feature an assortment of the following: supernatural/alien threats, strong language, upsetting scenes, violence, gore, blood, rape, suicide, monstrous menace, tobacco products, creature mayhem, psychological intimidation, sexual imagery, death, child endangerment, maiming, religious profanity, abusive behaviour, bullying, nudity, drug use, strobe lighting and racial stereotyping.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Please Note: This is an <strong>over 18’s</strong> event and no children are allowed entry.&nbsp;All sales are final.&nbsp;<strong>FrightFest does not refund tickets</strong>.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Please ensure you have read and agree to the FrightFest Code of Conduct before attending. This can be found here: <a href=\\\"https://www.frightfest.co.uk/conduct/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">https://www.frightfest.co.uk/conduct/</a></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>For any queries please contact: <a href=\\\"mailto:tickets@frightfest.co.uk\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">tickets@frightfest.co.uk</a>&nbsp;</p>\",\"ledger_tags\":[],\"rules\":[],\"terms_at_checkout\":\"<p>I confirm I am over 18. ID may be required. All sales are final and no refunds are given.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I have read and agree to the FrightFest Code of Conduct.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><a href=\\\"https://www.frightfest.co.uk/conduct/\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">https://www.frightfest.co.uk/conduct/</a></p>\"},{\"id\":\"6a5ea71346d929fd78f8b25b\",\"event_bucket\":\"6a17699850d66159f2035097\",\"timezone\":\"Europe/London\",\"name\":\"SHORT FILM SHOWCASE 4\",\"description\":\"\",\"short_description\":\"\",\"location\":\"ODEON Luxe West End - Discovery Screen 1\",\"venue\":{\"id\":\"6a53d8f172ba3569f93d018c\",\"name\":\"ODEON Luxe West End - Discovery Screen 1\",\"short_name\":\"Discovery Screen 1\",\"description\":\"\",\"address\":\"ODEON Luxe West End, 38a Leicester Square. London WC2H 7DX.\",\"default_capacity\":166,\"color\":\"#99c6ef\",\"use_reserved_seating\":true,\"comscore_include\":false,\"seatmap_id\":\"18b3da24-c60c-ecd9-f718-b6803037dd63\",\"seatmap_categories\":[{\"key\":\"1\",\"label\":\"House\",\"color\":\"#4176A5\",\"_id\":\"6a64966ab8d304b716d49458\"},{\"key\":\"2\",\"label\":\"House\",\"color\":\"#B2AFB0\",\"_id\":\"6a64966ab8d304b716d49459\"},{\"key\":\"3\",\"label\":\"Passholder Ticket\",\"color\":\"#FBA700\",\"_id\":\"6a64966ab8d304b716d4945a\"},{\"key\":\"4\",\"label\":\"Single Ticket\",\"color\":\"#F53F3F\",\"_id\":\"6a64966ab8d304b716d4945b\"}]},\"is_dated\":true,\"start_time\":\"2026-08-31T12:05:00.000Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-31T14:05:00.000Z\",\"cutoff_event_watch_at_availability_end\":false,\"tags\":[],\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"hide_tickets_button\":false,\"require_mailing_address\":false,\"require_phone_number\":false,\"rush_line_enabled\":true,\"passholder_ticket_required\":true,\"standalone_ticket_sales_enabled\":true,\"standalone_ticket_sales_unlocked\":false,\"sales_disabled_unless_coupon\":false,\"show_custom_checkout_message\":false,\"disable_pass_quick_order\":false,\"credits_disabled\":false,\"tickets_available\":true,\"unlimited\":false,\"quantity\":166,\"ticket_buckets\":[{\"id\":\"6a5ea71346d929fd78f8b25e\",\"name\":\"Single Ticket\",\"price\":1499,\"unlimited\":false,\"quantity\":119,\"quantity_sold\":99,\"quantity_scanned\":0,\"quantity_remaining\":20,\"reserved_seating_category\":\"4\",\"public\":true,\"autoissue_companion_ticket\":[],\"exclude_capacity\":false,\"lock_admin_only\":false,\"variable_price\":false,\"variable_price_minimum\":0,\"variants\":[],\"applicable_pass_buckets\":[],\"is_active\":true,\"virtual_intervals\":null},{\"id\":\"6a5fbd4af467aa15501d9a5e\",\"name\":\"Passholder Ticket\",\"price\":0,\"unlimited\":false,\"quantity\":39,\"quantity_sold\":39,\"quantity_scanned\":0,\"quantity_remaining\":0,\"reserved_seating_category\":\"3\",\"public\":true,\"autoissue_companion_ticket\":[],\"exclude_capacity\":false,\"lock_admin_only\":false,\"variable_price\":false,\"variable_price_minimum\":0,\"variants\":[],\"applicable_pass_buckets\":[\"6a804e190a759551798b743a\",\"6a858c3f365982c54a60687e\"],\"is_active\":true,\"virtual_intervals\":null}],\"films\":[{\"id\":\"6a5e1af9ae9bbda67f65e09e\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"6a17699850d66159f2035097\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"FrightFest 2026\",\"owner_id\":\"5dd16a51cb714c002f548a83\",\"name\":\"SHORT FILM SHOWCASE 4\",\"sort_key\":\"SHORT FILM SHOWCASE 4\",\"description\":\"<p><strong>Call Centre Shiva (UK Premiere)</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Director: Dylan Delaney.&nbsp;With: Jacqui Whelan, Brenda McSweeney.&nbsp;IRELAND 2026.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>16min.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>A beloved villager is accused of serial murder. However, the community have trouble reconciling the suspect's light and shadow side.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>THEMES OF SUICIDE</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Decorum (World Premiere)</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Director: Quentin Beroud.&nbsp;With: Jonny Labey, Margherita Barbieri.&nbsp;UK 2025. 9min.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>A perfect first date turns sour when Miles brings Angie back to his flat and she realises it's totally blank. But is zero decoration just laziness… or something darker?&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Crak Hack (UK Premiere)</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Director: Brendan Cleaves.&nbsp;With: Johnny Vivash.&nbsp;UK 2025.&nbsp;12min.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>In a near-future dominated by VR intimacy, a lonely man’s attempt to save his long-distance relationship with a high-tech device spirals into absurd and horrifying chaos when hackers seize control, forcing him to confront unspeakable scenarios in a desperate bid to regain his life.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>The Test (World Premiere)</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Director: Grattan Aikins.&nbsp;With: Laura Hutchinson, Culann McCarthy.&nbsp;IRELAND 2026.&nbsp;9min.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>A woman, Eve, wakes up groggy and disorientated in a room with nothing more than a bed and a chair. A voice over the loudspeakers begins to ask her a series of questions as a scientific test. Over a series of tests, Eve’s patience wears thin, and her inability to respond to the questions the way the company requires her leads to a final act of defiance in the face of her prisoners.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>I Spy (World Premiere)</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Director: David Yorke.&nbsp;With: Emma Louise Webb, Ellis Jordan.&nbsp;UK 2026.&nbsp;7min.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>An innocent game of I Spy between Julie and Ethan turns into a nightmare when an unseen presence joins the game.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Hope This Finds You Well (World Premiere)</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Director: Ben Ngondo-Cooke.&nbsp;With: Sonja Doubleday, Ginger, Ben Valentine Ngondo-Cooke.&nbsp;UK 2026.&nbsp;8min.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Private Investigator Gregory looks into the disappearance of Robin Ings, an employee of Naphtha Corporation.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Robin’s wife, Mrs Mildred Ings, seems to be involved in his absence and has taken over his correspondence.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The found footage captured by the doomed private investigator reveals the piggish horror within the Ings household.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>STROBE WARNING</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Baxter Hammond: P.I. (London Premiere)</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Director: Scott McCartney. With: Owen Coomber, Michael Moretti, Lauren Moore.&nbsp;UK 2025.&nbsp;10min.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Baxter Hammond, a professional paranormal investigator specialising in cases of supernatural disturbance. With the assistance of his trainee, Danny, he deals with exorcisms, werewolves, vampires, and group therapy for his monstrous clientele. He approaches each situation with composure and professional detachment — a man fulfilling his duties with quiet conviction and little else.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Sundowning (World Premiere)</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Director: Aimie Willemse.&nbsp;With: Betty Pirie, Maria Macdonnel, Sarah McCardie.&nbsp;UK 2026.&nbsp;11min.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Left alone with her estranged grandmother, a perceptive nine-year-old sees her become something monstrous, navigating a night of fear, confusion, and the thin line between love and survival.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>The Sorrows of Young Charlotte (World Premiere)</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Director: Shir Ariya. With: Liv Jekyll, Fabian Bevan. UK 2026.&nbsp;14min.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>After a devastating break-up, Charlie sleeps with her friend Werther on a whim.&nbsp;But when he confesses his true feelings for her, an unnerving and darkly explosive argument erupts.&nbsp;</p><p>.&nbsp;</p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1784763112728temp-1784763112721-cover.jpg\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"rating\":\"18\",\"runtime\":\"95\"},\"credits\":{},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-07-20T12:56:25.612Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-06T09:08:31.236Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true}],\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-19T11:48:06.750Z\",\"is_virtual\":false,\"comscore_include\":true,\"geographic_restrictions\":[],\"geographic_exclusions\":[],\"vague_geographic_restrictions\":false,\"show_in_coming_soon\":false,\"allow_preorder\":false,\"aarp_member_required\":false,\"show_quantity_countdown\":false,\"virtual_balloting_enabled\":false,\"virtual_balloting_inline_during_playback\":false,\"use_default_event_bucket_preroll\":true,\"virtual_content_preroll\":[],\"virtual_content_preroll_visible\":true,\"use_default_event_bucket_postroll\":true,\"virtual_content_postroll\":[],\"virtual_content_postroll_visible\":true,\"virtual_intervals\":null,\"display_ads\":[],\"images\":{},\"custom_email_text\":\"<p>Thank you for your order.&nbsp;Please find below your ticket. You just need to produce this on your phone where a member of our team will scan it.&nbsp;<strong>Please arrive on time – there are no trailers.&nbsp;Latecomers may be denied entry.</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>PLEASE NOTE:- FrightFest is a horror, fantasy, science fiction and thriller film based event for over 18s. Films shown will feature an assortment of the following: supernatural/alien threats, strong language, upsetting scenes, violence, gore, blood, rape, suicide, monstrous menace, tobacco products, creature mayhem, psychological intimidation, sexual imagery, death, child endangerment, maiming, religious profanity, abusive behaviour, bullying, nudity, drug use, strobe lighting and racial stereotyping.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Please Note: This is an <strong>over 18’s</strong> event and no children are allowed entry.&nbsp;All sales are final.&nbsp;<strong>FrightFest does not refund tickets</strong>.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Please ensure you have read and agree to the FrightFest Code of Conduct before attending. This can be found here: <a href=\\\"https://www.frightfest.co.uk/conduct/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">https://www.frightfest.co.uk/conduct/</a></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>For any queries please contact: <a href=\\\"mailto:tickets@frightfest.co.uk\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">tickets@frightfest.co.uk</a>&nbsp;</p>\",\"ledger_tags\":[],\"rules\":[],\"terms_at_checkout\":\"<p>I confirm I am over 18. ID may be required. All sales are final and no refunds are given.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I have read and agree to the FrightFest Code of Conduct.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><a href=\\\"https://www.frightfest.co.uk/conduct/\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">https://www.frightfest.co.uk/conduct/</a></p>\"},{\"id\":\"6a5ea70e46d929fd78f8b1fb\",\"event_bucket\":\"6a17699850d66159f2035097\",\"timezone\":\"Europe/London\",\"name\":\"VALLEY VIEW MOTEL\",\"description\":\"\",\"short_description\":\"\",\"location\":\"ODEON Luxe Leicester Square - Single Tickets\",\"venue\":{\"id\":\"6a53d79a6c5535dfd9936a4d\",\"name\":\"ODEON Luxe Leicester Square - Single Tickets\",\"short_name\":\"Main Screen - Single Tickets\",\"description\":\"\",\"address\":\"\",\"default_capacity\":57,\"color\":\"#f22313\",\"use_reserved_seating\":true,\"comscore_include\":false,\"seatmap_id\":\"aad0d885-2851-1b2a-2d4a-7ab95f4b7deb\",\"seatmap_categories\":[{\"key\":\"1\",\"label\":\"House\",\"color\":\"#B2AFB0\",\"_id\":\"6a6e3c9a1dde808a7926d17e\"},{\"key\":\"2\",\"label\":\"Single Ticket\",\"color\":\"#F53F3F\",\"_id\":\"6a6e3c9a1dde808a7926d17f\"}]},\"is_dated\":true,\"start_time\":\"2026-08-31T12:10:00.000Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-31T14:03:00.000Z\",\"cutoff_event_watch_at_availability_end\":false,\"tags\":[],\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"hide_tickets_button\":false,\"require_mailing_address\":false,\"require_phone_number\":false,\"rush_line_enabled\":true,\"passholder_ticket_required\":true,\"standalone_ticket_sales_enabled\":true,\"standalone_ticket_sales_unlocked\":false,\"sales_disabled_unless_coupon\":false,\"show_custom_checkout_message\":false,\"disable_pass_quick_order\":false,\"credits_disabled\":false,\"tickets_available\":true,\"unlimited\":true,\"quantity\":57,\"ticket_buckets\":[{\"id\":\"6a5ea70e46d929fd78f8b1fe\",\"name\":\"Single Ticket\",\"price\":1499,\"unlimited\":false,\"quantity\":57,\"quantity_sold\":15,\"quantity_scanned\":0,\"quantity_remaining\":42,\"reserved_seating_category\":\"2\",\"public\":true,\"autoissue_companion_ticket\":[],\"exclude_capacity\":false,\"lock_admin_only\":false,\"variable_price\":false,\"variable_price_minimum\":0,\"variants\":[],\"applicable_pass_buckets\":[],\"is_active\":true,\"virtual_intervals\":null}],\"films\":[{\"id\":\"6a5e1af9ae9bbda67f65e0d1\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"6a17699850d66159f2035097\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"FrightFest 2026\",\"owner_id\":\"5dd16a51cb714c002f548a83\",\"name\":\"VALLEY VIEW MOTEL\",\"sort_key\":\"VALLEY VIEW MOTEL\",\"description\":\"<p>From Kevin Ignatius and Nick Psinakis, the co-directors of the acclaimed 2023 FrightFest attraction CHEAT, comes a noir chiller in the tradition of early Coen Brothers. It’s 1977, and after a diamond heist goes seriously awry with multiple slaughters, two small-time crooks attempt to flee the wrath of the hitman put on their tail. Seeking refuge at a motel in the remote foothills of Pennsylvania run by a very peculiar owner and his sister, they have no idea what even grimmer hot mess they have stumbled into and soon must figure out a way to survive the night.</p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1784580088765temp-1784580088606-cover.jpg\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2026\",\"runtime\":\"93\",\"language\":\"ENGLISH\",\"country\":\"USA\",\"premiere\":\"World\",\"rating\":\"18\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Kevin Ignatius, Nick Psinakis\",\"cast\":\"Kevin Ignatius, Nick Psinakis, Melissa Collins, Laura Im\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-07-20T12:56:25.687Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-07-25T11:35:08.043Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true}],\"updated_at\":\"2026-07-25T10:40:39.726Z\",\"is_virtual\":false,\"comscore_include\":true,\"geographic_restrictions\":[],\"geographic_exclusions\":[],\"vague_geographic_restrictions\":false,\"show_in_coming_soon\":false,\"allow_preorder\":false,\"aarp_member_required\":false,\"show_quantity_countdown\":false,\"virtual_balloting_enabled\":false,\"virtual_balloting_inline_during_playback\":false,\"use_default_event_bucket_preroll\":true,\"virtual_content_preroll\":[],\"virtual_content_preroll_visible\":true,\"use_default_event_bucket_postroll\":true,\"virtual_content_postroll\":[],\"virtual_content_postroll_visible\":true,\"virtual_intervals\":null,\"display_ads\":[],\"images\":{},\"custom_email_text\":\"<p>Thank you for your order.&nbsp;Please find below your ticket. You just need to produce this on your phone where a member of our team will scan it.&nbsp;<strong>Please arrive on time – there are no trailers.&nbsp;Latecomers may be denied entry.</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>PLEASE NOTE:- FrightFest is a horror, fantasy, science fiction and thriller film based event for over 18s. Films shown will feature an assortment of the following: supernatural/alien threats, strong language, upsetting scenes, violence, gore, blood, rape, suicide, monstrous menace, tobacco products, creature mayhem, psychological intimidation, sexual imagery, death, child endangerment, maiming, religious profanity, abusive behaviour, bullying, nudity, drug use, strobe lighting and racial stereotyping.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Please Note: This is an <strong>over 18’s</strong> event and no children are allowed entry.&nbsp;All sales are final.&nbsp;<strong>FrightFest does not refund tickets</strong>.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Please ensure you have read and agree to the FrightFest Code of Conduct before attending. This can be found here: <a href=\\\"https://www.frightfest.co.uk/conduct/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">https://www.frightfest.co.uk/conduct/</a></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>For any queries please contact: <a href=\\\"mailto:tickets@frightfest.co.uk\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">tickets@frightfest.co.uk</a>&nbsp;</p>\",\"ledger_tags\":[],\"rules\":[],\"terms_at_checkout\":\"<p>I confirm I am over 18. ID may be required. All sales are final and no refunds are given.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I have read and agree to the FrightFest Code of Conduct.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><a href=\\\"https://www.frightfest.co.uk/conduct/\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">https://www.frightfest.co.uk/conduct/</a></p>\"},{\"id\":\"6a5ea71946d929fd78f8b2a9\",\"event_bucket\":\"6a17699850d66159f2035097\",\"timezone\":\"Europe/London\",\"name\":\"BLOOM\",\"description\":\"\",\"short_description\":\"\",\"location\":\"ODEON Luxe West End - Discovery Screen 2\",\"venue\":{