ikingly visual and emotionally-driven shocker graced by two fantastic central performances from Caylee Cowan and Tara Janae Smith. Living under the shadow of her late father's renowned literary legacy, aspiring artist Casey struggles to pen an original  horror novel while sharing a home with her increasingly erratic mother. As a budding friendship with the boy down the street, Steven, offers a glimpse beyond the walls of her isolated upbringing, long-buried tensions begin to surface, unraveling the fabric of her suffocated world and sharpening the complicated relationship she has with her mother. </p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1784579061594temp-1784579061458-cover.jpg\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2026\",\"runtime\":\"100\",\"language\":\"ENGLISH\",\"country\":\"USA\",\"premiere\":\"World\",\"rating\":\"18\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Carson McKinnon\",\"cast\":\"Caylee Cowan, Tara Janae Smith, Brady Noon, Isaac Akers\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-07-20T12:56:25.572Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-07-25T11:40:55.446Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true}],\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-19T12:16:10.938Z\",\"is_virtual\":false,\"comscore_include\":true,\"geographic_restrictions\":[],\"geographic_exclusions\":[],\"vague_geographic_restrictions\":false,\"show_in_coming_soon\":false,\"allow_preorder\":false,\"aarp_member_required\":false,\"show_quantity_countdown\":false,\"virtual_balloting_enabled\":false,\"virtual_balloting_inline_during_playback\":false,\"use_default_event_bucket_preroll\":true,\"virtual_content_preroll\":[],\"virtual_content_preroll_visible\":true,\"use_default_event_bucket_postroll\":true,\"virtual_content_postroll\":[],\"virtual_content_postroll_visible\":true,\"virtual_intervals\":null,\"display_ads\":[],\"images\":{},\"custom_email_text\":\"<p>Thank you for your order.&nbsp;Please find below your ticket. You just need to produce this on your phone where a member of our team will scan it.&nbsp;<strong>Please arrive on time – there are no trailers.&nbsp;Latecomers may be denied entry.</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>PLEASE NOTE:- FrightFest is a horror, fantasy, science fiction and thriller film based event for over 18s. Films shown will feature an assortment of the following: supernatural/alien threats, strong language, upsetting scenes, violence, gore, blood, rape, suicide, monstrous menace, tobacco products, creature mayhem, psychological intimidation, sexual imagery, death, child endangerment, maiming, religious profanity, abusive behaviour, bullying, nudity, drug use, strobe lighting and racial stereotyping.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Please Note: This is an <strong>over 18’s</strong> event and no children are allowed entry.&nbsp;All sales are final.&nbsp;<strong>FrightFest does not refund tickets</strong>.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Please ensure you have read and agree to the FrightFest Code of Conduct before attending. This can be found here: <a href=\\\"https://www.frightfest.co.uk/conduct/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">https://www.frightfest.co.uk/conduct/</a></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>For any queries please contact: <a href=\\\"mailto:tickets@frightfest.co.uk\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">tickets@frightfest.co.uk</a>&nbsp;</p>\",\"ledger_tags\":[],\"rules\":[],\"terms_at_checkout\":\"<p>I confirm I am over 18. ID may be required. All sales are final and no refunds are given.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I have read and agree to the FrightFest Code of Conduct.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><a href=\\\"https://www.frightfest.co.uk/conduct/\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">https://www.frightfest.co.uk/conduct/</a></p>\"},{\"id\":\"6a5ea70f46d929fd78f8b213\",\"event_bucket\":\"6a17699850d66159f2035097\",\"timezone\":\"Europe/London\",\"name\":\"SPECIES (SANGUINE)\",\"description\":\"\",\"short_description\":\"\",\"location\":\"ODEON Luxe Leicester Square - Single Tickets\",\"venue\":{\"id\":\"6a53d79a6c5535dfd9936a4d\",\"name\":\"ODEON Luxe Leicester Square - Single Tickets\",\"short_name\":\"Main Screen - Single Tickets\",\"description\":\"\",\"address\":\"\",\"default_capacity\":57,\"color\":\"#f22313\",\"use_reserved_seating\":true,\"comscore_include\":false,\"seatmap_id\":\"aad0d885-2851-1b2a-2d4a-7ab95f4b7deb\",\"seatmap_categories\":[{\"key\":\"1\",\"label\":\"House\",\"color\":\"#B2AFB0\",\"_id\":\"6a6e3c9a1dde808a7926d17e\"},{\"key\":\"2\",\"label\":\"Single Ticket\",\"color\":\"#F53F3F\",\"_id\":\"6a6e3c9a1dde808a7926d17f\"}]},\"is_dated\":true,\"start_time\":\"2026-08-31T19:55:00.000Z\",\"end_time\":\"2026-08-31T21:53:00.000Z\",\"cutoff_event_watch_at_availability_end\":false,\"tags\":[],\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"hide_tickets_button\":false,\"require_mailing_address\":false,\"require_phone_number\":false,\"rush_line_enabled\":true,\"passholder_ticket_required\":true,\"standalone_ticket_sales_enabled\":true,\"standalone_ticket_sales_unlocked\":false,\"sales_disabled_unless_coupon\":false,\"show_custom_checkout_message\":false,\"disable_pass_quick_order\":false,\"credits_disabled\":false,\"tickets_available\":true,\"unlimited\":true,\"quantity\":57,\"ticket_buckets\":[{\"id\":\"6a5ea70f46d929fd78f8b216\",\"name\":\"Single Ticket\",\"price\":1499,\"unlimited\":false,\"quantity\":57,\"quantity_sold\":58,\"quantity_scanned\":0,\"quantity_remaining\":0,\"reserved_seating_category\":\"2\",\"public\":true,\"autoissue_companion_ticket\":[],\"exclude_capacity\":false,\"lock_admin_only\":false,\"variable_price\":false,\"variable_price_minimum\":0,\"variants\":[],\"applicable_pass_buckets\":[],\"is_active\":true,\"virtual_intervals\":null}],\"films\":[{\"id\":\"6a5e1af9ae9bbda67f65e0a4\",\"type\":\"film\",\"event_bucket\":\"6a17699850d66159f2035097\",\"event_bucket_name\":\"FrightFest 2026\",\"owner_id\":\"5dd16a51cb714c002f548a83\",\"name\":\"SPECIES (SANGUINE)\",\"sort_key\":\"SPECIES (SANGUINE)\",\"description\":\"<p>A junior doctor falls victim to a mysterious, life-threatening sickness in French writer-director Marion Le Corroller’s debut feature, a darkly comic sci-fi body-horror thriller with a deeper allegorical message about workplace burn-out in high-pressure capitalist societies. Margot Loiseau (Mara Taquin), a young intern at the most competitive Emergency Room in the country, has trouble keeping up in this exhausting and anxiety-ridden environment. Hélène Vergile (Karin Viard), the experienced doctor in charge of the resident novices, is described by Margot’s fellow intern Louis (Sami Outalbali) as ‘the devil’, both for her extremely exacting attitude and for the way she plays the interns off against one another. Here life-and-death decisions must be made with accuracy and at speed and Margot, whose mother died owing to a faulty hospital diagnosis and who, unlike her colleague Pauline (Kim Higelin), was not born into a medical career, is soon crumbling under duress. As she’s confronted with multiple patients her age presenting unusual symptoms, her own body starts to show disturbing changes. An official world premiere screening in the cult-friendly Midnight section at this year’s Cannes Film Festival, SPECIES expands on Le Corroller’s 2020 short ‘No More God in Doctor’, and was partly inspired by her own experiences in a very stressful job in the financial market where it proved hard  to define her own identity. Citing her two cinematic gurus as Yorgos Lanthimos and Ari Aster for their imaginative boldness in making movies that cause audience discomfort, Le Corroller has stated her film’s extreme tone, broad satire, elevated genre elements, superlative visual effects, splatter violence and political subtext reflect her personality. With stand-out and unique body-mutation sequences created by special make-up effects designer Pierre-Olivier Persin, who won an Oscar for THE SUBSTANCE, SPECIES is an exciting and exhilarating Gen Z shocker and your next obsession.</p>\",\"cover_image\":\"https://static-a.eventive.org/1784762964362temp-1784762964350-cover.jpg\",\"unballoted\":false,\"details\":{\"year\":\"2026\",\"runtime\":\"103\",\"language\":\"France/Belgium\",\"country\":\"France/Belgium\",\"premiere\":\"UK\",\"rating\":\"18\",\"genre\":\"French/Belgian\",\"content_warning\":\"WARNING: This content contains flashing lights and high-contrast visuals that may cause discomfort or trigger seizures in people with photosensitive epilepsy. Viewer discretion is advised\"},\"credits\":{\"director\":\"Marion Le Corroller\",\"cast\":\"Mara Taquin, Karin Viard, Kim Higelin, Sami Outalbali\"},\"expanded_credits\":[],\"tags\":[{\"id\":\"6a5e1af9ae9bbda67f65e0a5\",\"name\":\"Closing Flim\",\"color\":\"#608ea4\",\"visible\":true}],\"comscore_include\":true,\"visibility\":\"visible\",\"created_at\":\"2026-07-20T12:56:25.619Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-07-25T11:38:32.509Z\",\"_use_beta_vod_flow_for_new_virtual_content\":true}],\"updated_at\":\"2026-07-25T10:43:50.709Z\",\"is_virtual\":false,\"comscore_include\":true,\"geographic_restrictions\":[],\"geographic_exclusions\":[],\"vague_geographic_restrictions\":false,\"show_in_coming_soon\":false,\"allow_preorder\":false,\"aarp_member_required\":false,\"show_quantity_countdown\":false,\"virtual_balloting_enabled\":false,\"virtual_balloting_inline_during_playback\":false,\"use_default_event_bucket_preroll\":true,\"virtual_content_preroll\":[],\"virtual_content_preroll_visible\":true,\"use_default_event_bucket_postroll\":true,\"virtual_content_postroll\":[],\"virtual_content_postroll_visible\":true,\"virtual_intervals\":null,\"display_ads\":[],\"images\":{},\"custom_email_text\":\"<p>Thank you for your order.&nbsp;Please find below your ticket. You just need to produce this on your phone where a member of our team will scan it.&nbsp;<strong>Please arrive on time – there are no trailers.&nbsp;Latecomers may be denied entry.</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>PLEASE NOTE:- FrightFest is a horror, fantasy, science fiction and thriller film based event for over 18s. Films shown will feature an assortment of the following: supernatural/alien threats, strong language, upsetting scenes, violence, gore, blood, rape, suicide, monstrous menace, tobacco products, creature mayhem, psychological intimidation, sexual imagery, death, child endangerment, maiming, religious profanity, abusive behaviour, bullying, nudity, drug use, strobe lighting and racial stereotyping.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Please Note: This is an <strong>over 18’s</strong> event and no children are allowed entry.&nbsp;All sales are final.&nbsp;<strong>FrightFest does not refund tickets</strong>.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Please ensure you have read and agree to the FrightFest Code of Conduct before attending. This can be found here: <a href=\\\"https://www.frightfest.co.uk/conduct/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">https://www.frightfest.co.uk/conduct/</a></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>For any queries please contact: <a href=\\\"mailto:tickets@frightfest.co.uk\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">tickets@frightfest.co.uk</a>&nbsp;</p>\",\"ledger_tags\":[],\"rules\":[],\"terms_at_checkout\":\"<p>I confirm I am over 18. ID may be required. All sales are final and no refunds are given.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I have read and agree to the FrightFest Code of Conduct.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><a href=\\\"https://www.frightfest.co.uk/conduct/\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">https://www.frightfest.co.uk/conduct/</a></p>\"}],\"includes_all_events\":false}",
